  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 247 AM CDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nThrough early next week (Tuesday)...\n\nToday (Wednesday): RAP/water vapor analysis indicates upper low \nis situated northern GA and corner of the Carolinas this morning \nand 595DM mid level ridge over the Desert Southwest, leading to \ncontinued northerly dry flow across the Gulf Coast states. This \nlocks in PWs generally around one inch (1.1 to 1.3 inches) and \nlow humidity aloft (i.e. 700-300mb layer humidity in the low teens\nto single digits) and another day of efficient mixing. This leads\nto moderating temperatures: highs becoming seasonably warm into \nWednesday (93F to 97F) and seasonable lows (68F to 71F this \nmorning to 70F to 74F Wednesday night). Heat indices will\ngradually increase today in southwestern areas (heat indices in \nthe 102F to 105F range this afternoon). Inherited HWO graphic for\nLimited heat in southwest  today seems reasonable. Cannot rule \nout a stray shower in the extreme southwest MS and northeast LA \nwhere deep moisture will be higher and diurnally induced \nconvection may develop. \n\nLate week into early next week (Thursday through next Tuesday):\nAs the upper low weakens the grip over the Southeast beginning\ntomorrow, low level southerly return flow and an uptick in\nmoisture (low and deep layer moisture) will favor less efficient\nmixing, warmth/moist advection and increasing heat stress late\nweek through the weekend. Mixing on Thursday will be increased in\ncentral to northeast MS where low humidity aloft will reside.\nTemperatures will be seasonably warm (highs in the 94F to 97F\nrange and lows in the 72F to 76F range). The region will remain in\nmore of a large scale weakness in the flow but low level flow will\nhelp moderate in higher surface dewpoints into the weekend (72F to\n76F) and increasing heat stress concerns. With inherited HWO\ngraphic of lower threat today than Thursday into weekend, decided\nto go ahead with an HWO graphic into the weekend. Will likely\ndepict a larger threat area to show an expanding concern and \nlikely areawide into the weekend. Further adjustments, expansions \nand heat headlines will likely be needed.\n\nLow level moist advection and increased deep moisture aloft will\nincrease Thursday and into the weekend (PWs in the 1.5 to 2 inch \nrange by the weekend into early next week). Rain chances will \nmainly be summertime variety (diurnally induced) Thursday south of\nInterstate 20 and along and southeast of Natchez Trace into the\nweekend and spreading northwest into early next week. Coverage \nwill be isolated to at times scattered coverage (20 to 45 percent \nrange) to a little more numerous in the Pine Belt early next week\nfrom deep moisture (PWs in excess of 2.0 inches) and potentially \nsea breeze influence. This pattern will not favor any noteworthy \nstorm threat, but a few scattered stronger gusty storms with \nlocally heavy rain cannot be ruled out, especially late weekend \ninto early next week. /DC/",
